>>__ load "simpExtLib";
>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `prepare_rewrite_bundle`

``` hol4
simpExtLib.prepare_rewrite_arguments :
  simpExtLib.simpset -> thm list -> simpExtLib.simpset * thm list
simpExtLib.prepare_rewrite_bundle :
  simpExtLib.simpset -> thm list -> simpExtLib.rewrite_bundle
simpExtLib.rewrite_bundle_rules : simpExtLib.rewrite_bundle ->
  (thm * simpExtLib.rewrite_source list) list
simpExtLib.combine_rewrite_bundles :
  simpExtLib.rewrite_bundle list -> simpExtLib.rewrite_bundle
simpExtLib.install_rewrite_bundle : simpExtLib.rewrite_bundle ->
  (simpExtLib.rewrite_source * thm) list ->
  simpExtLib.simpset -> simpExtLib.simpset
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Prepares supplied rewrites once for an extension invocation, so nested
consumers and associated views can share their actual compiled controls.

First use `prepare_rewrite_arguments ss ths` to apply directives and obtain
an extension set and plain supplied rules. This is explicit construction:
it can install fragments, replay history and run makers/collectors.
Compatible surviving installed sources retain their actual controls,
including partially spent or exhausted counters. It never imports an
ordinary simpset. Requirements and other tactic-only processing still
belong to the tactic layer.

`prepare_rewrite_bundle base rules` compiles supplied rules without
installing them or priming ambient reducers. `rewrite_bundle_rules` exposes
the supplied rules with their compiled source handles for view derivation.
`install_rewrite_bundle bundle views base` installs the binding and any
attached views. Install it **once per simpset**; pass the same installed
binding to nested consumers rather than supplying its rules again.

`combine_rewrite_bundles` combines existing compiled bindings without
refreshing quotas or origins and rejects duplicate bindings. Installation
retains each constituent event. History replay retains cached compiled
shapes without rerunning their rewrite maker. Ordinary reset replay resets
declared quotas while retaining conjunct sharing; explicit
control-preserving replay keeps the compatible sources' actual remaining
uses. Extracting either traversal projection never resets those controls.

The `GEN_GLOBAL_SIMP_TAC_CHILD_FIRST_BOUND` tactic expects the bundle to be
already installed in its invocation simpset. Its last theorem-list argument
is for local directives, not another copy of the bundle's rules. It retains
the untagged solver context and does not reinstall/recompile the bundle.

### Failure

Argument processing, compilation and callbacks can fail. Duplicate bundle
bindings/installations and invalid attached views are rejected.

### Example

``` hol4
>>_ val ext_bool_ss = simpExtLib.lift_simpset boolSimps.bool_ss;
>>_ val (base, rules) = simpExtLib.prepare_rewrite_arguments
     ext_bool_ss [BoundedRewrites.Once boolTheory.AND_CLAUSES];
>>_ val bundle : simpExtLib.rewrite_bundle =
     simpExtLib.prepare_rewrite_bundle base rules;
>>_ val invocation : simpExtLib.simpset =
     simpExtLib.install_rewrite_bundle bundle [] base;
>> simpExtLib.SIMP_CONV invocation [] “T ∧ p”;
```

